cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SHAARP.py
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the two ♯SHAARP papers below, which
  introduced the methods SHAARP.py implements.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/Rui-Zu/SHAARP.py
url: https://shaarp-py.readthedocs.io
abstract: >-
  SHAARP.py simulates and fits optical second-harmonic generation (SHG) in
  anisotropic crystals and thin-film multilayers. It is a free, open-source
  Python package and a standalone desktop app that brings the two published
  ♯SHAARP methods together: SHAARP.si for reflected SHG polarimetry from a
  single crystal surface, and SHAARP.ml for multilayers and Maker fringes with
  complete multiple reflections. On top of the two methods it adds closed-form
  symbolic SHG expressions, d-tensor extraction from polarimetry scans, an
  N-layer stack editor and a scriptable API. The solvers are checked against
  the published equations and the reference output of the original packages.
keywords:
  - second harmonic generation
  - nonlinear optics
  - anisotropic crystals
  - Maker fringes
  - polarimetry
  - ferroelectrics
